1
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:36,500
Hercules Formation, abort mission.

2
00:00:36,583 --> 00:00:39,208
Negative. We can't return without Hyena 2.

3
00:00:39,291 --> 00:00:41,000
Hercules 1, it is too risky.

4
00:00:41,083 --> 00:00:42,833
There are Stingers out there, Hercules.

5
00:00:43,333 --> 00:00:45,791
Nishi is alone.
I won't come back until I've found him.

6
00:00:45,875 --> 00:00:47,125
Deviating from your planned mission.

7
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,208
Stinger spotted.

8
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:18,458
Chief, there's some good news.

9
00:01:19,041 --> 00:01:22,250
We have shot down
an Indian Air Force jet in Kargil.

10
00:01:22,958 --> 00:01:24,375
Excellent.

11
00:01:25,583 --> 00:01:27,208
Now let's see

12
00:01:27,291 --> 00:01:31,083
how many more pilots the Indian Air Force
will send to their deaths.

13
00:02:23,125 --> 00:02:26,541
For the last 52 years,
the India-Pakistan border

14
00:02:26,625 --> 00:02:28,541
has been engulfed by war,
suspicion, and mistrust.

15
00:02:29,791 --> 00:02:33,333
And last year, when the two countries
conducted nuclear tests,

16
00:02:33,416 --> 00:02:36,125
this mistrust reached its peak.

17
00:02:36,208 --> 00:02:40,750
It was called the most dangerous event
in the world after World War II.

18
00:02:40,833 --> 00:02:44,208
But just seven months later,
Prime Minister Atal Bihari Vajpayee

19
00:02:44,291 --> 00:02:47,208
accepted Nawaz Sharif's invitation,

20
00:02:47,291 --> 00:02:50,250
and announced the historic
Lahore Bus Yatra.

21
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:51,916
Now the question is,

22
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,833
"Will the defense forces of both countries
be able to trust this peace?"

23
00:03:10,416 --> 00:03:13,166
Gentlemen, peace or no peace.

24
00:03:13,250 --> 00:03:16,083
This year too, the Western Air Command's
war game exercise

25
00:03:16,166 --> 00:03:17,666
will take place as scheduled.

26
00:03:17,750 --> 00:03:20,875
Like every year,
this will be a test of your flying skills,

27
00:03:20,958 --> 00:03:23,291
alertness, innovation,

28
00:03:23,375 --> 00:03:24,708
and bravery.

29
00:03:24,791 --> 00:03:27,958
This year too, all the squadrons
will be split into two teams.

30
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:30,500
Red Land and Blue Land.

31
00:03:30,583 --> 00:03:31,583
But this year,

32
00:03:31,666 --> 00:03:33,375
for the first time,

33
00:03:33,458 --> 00:03:34,375
in Blue Land,

34
00:03:34,458 --> 00:03:36,666
a Photo Recce Squadron
will also be involved.

35
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:39,500
Golden Arrows,
led by Wing Commander Tony Dhanoa,

36
00:03:39,583 --> 00:03:42,833
who will conduct reconnaissance
for the bomb squadron Wolfpack,

37
00:03:42,916 --> 00:03:44,625
identify targets,

38
00:03:44,708 --> 00:03:47,208
and assess post-strike damage.

39
00:03:47,291 --> 00:03:48,958
In the next month,

40
00:03:49,541 --> 00:03:51,416
there will be five operational rounds,

41
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:53,166
then the semi-finals,

42
00:03:53,250 --> 00:03:54,375
and finals.

43
00:03:54,458 --> 00:03:55,458
Any questions?

44
00:03:55,541 --> 00:03:56,708
No, sir!

45
00:03:56,791 --> 00:04:00,666
Gentlemen, before this exercise,
I asked you all,

46
00:04:01,291 --> 00:04:04,625
"How will you ensure
your squadrons are war-ready?"

47
00:04:04,708 --> 00:04:06,916
And I have received your requirements.

48
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,708
Jammer pods,

49
00:04:08,791 --> 00:04:10,458
self-defense system,

50
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:12,875
advanced flying simulators.

51
00:04:12,958 --> 00:04:16,583
And someone even asked
for night-vision goggles.

52
00:04:17,166 --> 00:04:19,166
But, Tony,

53
00:04:20,666 --> 00:04:22,541
you haven't asked for a thing.

54
00:04:23,125 --> 00:04:24,333
Sir, in my squadron,

55
00:04:24,416 --> 00:04:27,291
I have some of the youngest fighter pilots
of the Western Air Command.

56
00:04:28,041 --> 00:04:29,166
They're academy-trained,

57
00:04:29,250 --> 00:04:31,875
but it's their first time
flying the MiG-21 operationally.

58
00:04:32,458 --> 00:04:34,000
Sir, you and I both know

59
00:04:34,083 --> 00:04:37,666
MiG-21 has the fastest take-off
and landing speed in the world.

60
00:04:37,750 --> 00:04:39,125
Before they become war-ready,

61
00:04:39,208 --> 00:04:41,708
I want my boys to be MiG-ready.

62
00:04:42,875 --> 00:04:44,958
And for that, we don't need any equipment.

63
00:04:45,958 --> 00:04:47,916
We need a good coach.

64
00:04:48,750 --> 00:04:50,541
And who is this coach?

65
00:04:52,416 --> 00:04:54,291
Squadron Leader Ajay Ahuja.

66
00:04:54,958 --> 00:04:58,458
I can't think of a better name than him
to turn my boys into men.

67
00:05:07,625 --> 00:05:08,833
Sorry, Alka.

68
00:05:10,250 --> 00:05:12,166
We need to keep moving because of me.

69
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:14,500
"Sorry"?

70
00:05:16,666 --> 00:05:18,291
I was about to say thank you.

71
00:05:19,416 --> 00:05:20,250
"Thank you," why?

72
00:05:20,833 --> 00:05:22,541
For so many new sarees.

73
00:05:24,250 --> 00:05:25,541
At a new posting,

74
00:05:26,541 --> 00:05:28,791
even old sarees become new.

75
00:05:39,375 --> 00:05:40,333
Hey, champion.

76
00:05:41,375 --> 00:05:42,708
Come on, tell me.

77
00:05:42,791 --> 00:05:43,750
Fourteen eights are?

78
00:05:46,541 --> 00:05:48,583
-One, one, two.
-Too slow.

79
00:05:49,666 --> 00:05:51,125
Do you want to become
a fighter pilot or not?

80
00:05:51,208 --> 00:05:54,250
A fighter pilot has to solve math problems
in a second.

81
00:05:56,041 --> 00:05:58,250
1700 hours. Be ready.

82
00:05:58,333 --> 00:06:00,416
There's an even bigger swimming pool here.

83
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:01,583
Okay, Dad.

84
00:06:02,166 --> 00:06:03,125
-Bye.
-Bye.

85
00:06:06,916 --> 00:06:08,333
You have become a flight commander,

86
00:06:08,416 --> 00:06:10,791
at least buy a decent bike.

87
00:06:14,875 --> 00:06:16,791
I have 16 MiGs, ma'am.

88
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:59,208
If the Flight Commander rides in
on a scooter from the Stone Age,

89
00:06:59,291 --> 00:07:01,458
what impression will it make on the boys?

90
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:04,375
Sir, why is everyone
obsessed with my scooter?

91
00:07:05,250 --> 00:07:06,916
In any case, if you come to think of it,

92
00:07:07,750 --> 00:07:10,250
our MiGs are older than my scooter.

93
00:07:11,333 --> 00:07:12,250
Right, Tony sir?

94
00:07:12,333 --> 00:07:14,250
You and your twisted logic.

95
00:07:14,333 --> 00:07:15,750
Come here. Come.

96
00:07:16,833 --> 00:07:18,666
Welcome to Golden Arrows.

97
00:07:19,583 --> 00:07:21,916
-Good to see you again, Ahuja.
-Thank you, sir.

98
00:07:24,791 --> 00:07:25,875
Oh, wow.

99
00:07:26,583 --> 00:07:28,041
Annual war game exercise, sir.

100
00:07:28,125 --> 00:07:29,500
Semi-finals.

101
00:07:30,083 --> 00:07:32,625
It's time for the boys
to meet their new coach.

102
00:07:33,916 --> 00:07:36,333
As the dedicated photo recce squadron,

103
00:07:36,916 --> 00:07:39,041
our job is to approach the target,

104
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:41,166
fly low and take photos.

105
00:07:41,250 --> 00:07:43,416
Then enlarge these photos

106
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:46,083
and share the exact strike coordinates
with the bombing squadron.

107
00:07:46,166 --> 00:07:50,333
As soon as you cross this make-shift LoC,
the timer will start.

108
00:07:50,416 --> 00:07:52,250
Forty-five seconds.

109
00:07:52,333 --> 00:07:54,916
If you haven't returned within 45 seconds,

110
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:57,125
Red Land's surface-to-air missiles

111
00:07:57,208 --> 00:07:58,500
will lock on to you,

112
00:07:58,583 --> 00:08:01,333
and for all practical purposes,
you're dead,

113
00:08:01,416 --> 00:08:03,500
and we'll lose points.

114
00:08:03,583 --> 00:08:05,500
And that cannot happen.

115
00:08:07,041 --> 00:08:08,083
-Jai Hind, sir.
-Jai Hind.

116
00:08:09,125 --> 00:08:10,208
At ease, Arrows.

117
00:08:14,916 --> 00:08:17,375
I want you
to meet your new flight commander.

118
00:08:18,166 --> 00:08:20,166
Squadron Leader Ajay Ahuja.

119
00:08:20,250 --> 00:08:21,916
Ajay was supposed to join us tomorrow.

120
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,541
But I guess he was dying to see you guys.

121
00:08:24,625 --> 00:08:27,375
What do you think our strategy should be?

122
00:08:27,458 --> 00:08:29,916
The enemy will have missiles, sir.

123
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,583
We must fly the mission in radio silence.

124
00:08:32,666 --> 00:08:34,208
I am not talking about that mission.

125
00:08:34,291 --> 00:08:39,250
I'm talking about the India-Pakistan
peace summit on 19th February.

126
00:08:39,333 --> 00:08:40,875
For the first time in 52 years,

127
00:08:40,958 --> 00:08:44,708
our prime minister
will be going to Pakistan by road.

128
00:08:45,333 --> 00:08:48,416
What are your thoughts
about this bus trip?

129
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:50,333
I think this is a good step, sir.

130
00:08:50,916 --> 00:08:52,416
Both have nuclear weapons.

131
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,416
It's very important
to find a permanent solution.

132
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:56,875
Sir, a permanent solution is impossible.

133
00:08:56,958 --> 00:08:59,958
-Tensions may subside a little, that's it.
-How?

134
00:09:00,041 --> 00:09:01,291
Mistake.

135
00:09:03,333 --> 00:09:04,625
This is a big mistake, sir.

136
00:09:04,708 --> 00:09:07,041
A country like Pakistan cannot be trusted.

137
00:09:07,125 --> 00:09:09,125
Peace is also necessary
between India and Pakistan.

138
00:09:09,208 --> 00:09:11,708
The other country should also have
the same intention, right, Baldy?

139
00:09:11,791 --> 00:09:13,416
Ahuja, what do you think?

140
00:09:14,625 --> 00:09:16,333
Sir, I don't think about all this.

141
00:09:16,416 --> 00:09:17,500
Exactly!

142
00:09:18,125 --> 00:09:21,708
You shouldn't even think about it.
Politics is not the Air Force's concern.

143
00:09:21,791 --> 00:09:23,291
We are razor blades.

144
00:09:23,375 --> 00:09:27,375
We are trained to cut,
not to think about all this.

145
00:09:27,875 --> 00:09:29,458
We are 17 points behind.

146
00:09:30,083 --> 00:09:32,333
If you don't get 20 points
in the semi-finals,

147
00:09:32,958 --> 00:09:35,458
no matter how many
fancy maneuvers you do,

148
00:09:35,541 --> 00:09:36,750
Red land will end up winning.

149
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:41,083
Chou.

150
00:09:41,833 --> 00:09:42,916
Boys for the mission?

151
00:09:43,458 --> 00:09:44,708
Dhali and Goofy.

152
00:09:45,416 --> 00:09:46,333
Boys,

153
00:09:46,416 --> 00:09:50,250
this is the closest you will get
to experiencing war.

154
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:53,250
It's a war you've never lost, sir.

155
00:09:53,333 --> 00:09:55,541
And I will not lose this time either.

156
00:09:57,958 --> 00:09:59,333
Go get me those points.

157
00:09:59,416 --> 00:10:00,666
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

158
00:10:35,708 --> 00:10:37,208
Long live Pakistan, sir.

159
00:10:37,291 --> 00:10:38,583
Long live.

160
00:10:43,875 --> 00:10:45,416
Sir, what brings you here?

161
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:47,041
The World Cup is around the corner,

162
00:10:47,125 --> 00:10:49,375
so I thought I'd give the players
a little encouragement.

163
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:53,208
Anyway, there's hardly any difference
between players and soldiers.

164
00:10:53,791 --> 00:10:55,833
We are always fighting for the next war.

165
00:10:55,916 --> 00:10:57,083
Very true, sir.

166
00:10:59,083 --> 00:11:00,541
Junaid was six years old.

167
00:11:00,625 --> 00:11:02,833
Even then he wanted
to become a fast bowler.

168
00:11:04,375 --> 00:11:06,750
Sir, you still remember?

169
00:11:08,458 --> 00:11:09,458
Of course, Tauqir.

170
00:11:11,666 --> 00:11:13,000
Inshallah, he will soon play

171
00:11:13,083 --> 00:11:15,208
for Pakistan's cricket team too.

172
00:11:15,916 --> 00:11:18,125
How, sir? With Younis, Akhtar…

173
00:11:18,875 --> 00:11:21,666
Akram and all in the mix,
it is difficult, sir.

174
00:11:24,250 --> 00:11:25,833
Tauqir sahib,

175
00:11:25,916 --> 00:11:27,416
when his own father

176
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:30,250
is set to become the chairman
of the Pakistan Cricket Board,

177
00:11:30,833 --> 00:11:32,166
what difficulty will he face?

178
00:11:32,250 --> 00:11:33,125
Sir?

179
00:11:33,208 --> 00:11:35,166
A new PCB chairman
will be elected in December.

180
00:11:35,250 --> 00:11:38,291
For this post, who could be better than

181
00:11:38,375 --> 00:11:40,708
the Pakistan Army's star sportsperson?

182
00:11:44,833 --> 00:11:47,208
Sir, the Pakistan team
is a big responsibility.

183
00:11:53,791 --> 00:11:55,500
Are you afraid to take on responsibility?

184
00:11:56,708 --> 00:11:57,708
No, sir.

185
00:11:59,250 --> 00:12:02,000
Can you get Pakistan another World Cup?

186
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,041
I will try, sir.

187
00:12:12,458 --> 00:12:16,583
Then surely you'll also get Kashmir
for Pakistan?

188
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,041
Kashmir, sir?

189
00:12:23,375 --> 00:12:25,000
Every year, the armies of both countries

190
00:12:25,083 --> 00:12:28,208
descend from
the snowy mountain peaks of Kashmir,

191
00:12:28,291 --> 00:12:30,125
as per the Simla Agreement.

192
00:12:30,791 --> 00:12:35,375
And as DGMO, it is your office
that gives these orders, right?

193
00:12:36,916 --> 00:12:37,791
Right, sir.

194
00:12:38,375 --> 00:12:41,333
But this time,
our soldiers will not descend.

195
00:12:44,333 --> 00:12:46,958
But, sir, this is a violation
of the Simla Agreement--

196
00:12:47,041 --> 00:12:48,791
This is also
a direct violation of the LoC.

197
00:12:48,875 --> 00:12:51,625
Because this time,
our soldiers will go forward.

198
00:12:51,708 --> 00:12:53,958
To capture all those posts across the LoC

199
00:12:54,041 --> 00:12:58,000
that India will have vacated,
honoring the agreement.

200
00:12:58,625 --> 00:12:59,958
Especially those posts

201
00:13:00,041 --> 00:13:02,291
from where India's National Highway 1

202
00:13:03,041 --> 00:13:05,708
will be in our direct line of sight.

203
00:13:07,333 --> 00:13:08,666
But, sir,

204
00:13:08,750 --> 00:13:11,333
Mian sahib is about to begin
peace talks with India.

205
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:13,000
So?

206
00:13:14,500 --> 00:13:15,625
Pardon me, sir.

207
00:13:16,708 --> 00:13:18,958
Is the Prime Minister aware
of this operation?

208
00:13:23,125 --> 00:13:25,500
It's an army operation, General Zia.

209
00:13:27,416 --> 00:13:29,666
What is the need for Mian sahib in this?

210
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:38,791
Are the posters for the peace talks ready?

211
00:13:38,875 --> 00:13:40,000
Sir, the layout is ready.

212
00:13:40,083 --> 00:13:42,916
Is the meeting with
Faiz sahib's daughter fixed?

213
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,541
No, sir. He's--

214
00:13:44,625 --> 00:13:47,500
Vajpayee sahib is a great admirer of Faiz.

215
00:13:48,541 --> 00:13:50,375
This should be looked into on priority.

216
00:13:50,458 --> 00:13:51,541
Yes, sir.

217
00:13:52,750 --> 00:13:54,416
Sir, your father's asking for you.

218
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,750
The cabinet has been waiting for a while.

219
00:13:58,541 --> 00:14:00,958
This is filled with mistakes.

220
00:14:02,250 --> 00:14:03,416
Mr. Aqil,

221
00:14:04,583 --> 00:14:07,166
Vajpayee sahib will be
the first Indian prime minister

222
00:14:07,250 --> 00:14:09,083
to set foot in Minar-e-Pakistan.

223
00:14:09,875 --> 00:14:11,500
Understand the significance
of these talks.

224
00:14:11,583 --> 00:14:12,916
-Okay, I'll come.
-Yes, sir.

225
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:13,916
Please be seated, everyone.

226
00:14:17,333 --> 00:14:19,791
So, what is the agenda
for today's meeting?

227
00:14:20,625 --> 00:14:22,708
-The peace talks only, sir.
-Really?

228
00:14:23,416 --> 00:14:26,458
Our suggestion is that during the talks,

229
00:14:26,541 --> 00:14:30,375
we propose the Chenab River
as the new Line of Control.

230
00:14:31,875 --> 00:14:32,708
This…

231
00:14:33,541 --> 00:14:35,291
The LoC will be like this,

232
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:38,291
visible even from the moon.

233
00:14:51,333 --> 00:14:53,541
We've talked about this before,
haven't we?

234
00:14:55,750 --> 00:15:00,708
India will never accept this
80-20 division in Pakistan's favor.

235
00:15:00,791 --> 00:15:01,916
Sir,

236
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:06,000
the Chenab River evenly divides the Hindu
and Muslim populations of Kashmir.

237
00:15:06,708 --> 00:15:09,166
-It's the ideal solution to the conflict.
-Aziz sahib.

238
00:15:10,250 --> 00:15:12,708
I'm the one
speaking to Vajpayee sahib every day.

239
00:15:13,750 --> 00:15:15,083
He will never agree to this.

240
00:15:15,166 --> 00:15:16,291
Nawaz…

241
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:21,333
By all means, do keep up
your friendly chats with him.

242
00:15:22,166 --> 00:15:26,458
But in the "real" negotiations,
follow Aziz sahib's lead.

243
00:15:29,833 --> 00:15:34,750
When it comes to diplomatic talks,
he has far more experience than all of us.

244
00:15:37,416 --> 00:15:38,375
Yes, Abba ji.

245
00:15:41,416 --> 00:15:43,666
Should we move on to India's draft, sir?

246
00:15:45,125 --> 00:15:47,208
What is your opinion on this, Aziz sahib?

247
00:15:52,666 --> 00:15:56,875
Sir, the Chief has appointed his loyalists
to all key army positions.

248
00:15:56,958 --> 00:15:57,791
So?

249
00:15:58,833 --> 00:16:01,958
Sir, our political history shows that,

250
00:16:02,041 --> 00:16:05,291
whenever the army has expanded its reach,
the outcome has not been good.

251
00:16:05,375 --> 00:16:08,541
Butt sahib, I bypassed three seniors
and made him Army Chief.

252
00:16:10,166 --> 00:16:13,333
Now, if he wants to savor the feeling
of being chief, let him.

253
00:16:13,875 --> 00:16:14,750
How does it matter?

254
00:16:14,833 --> 00:16:16,666
Sir, this is a matter of border positions.

255
00:16:16,750 --> 00:16:19,083
If the chief tries anything reckless
in the valley,

256
00:16:19,166 --> 00:16:22,375
the ISI's long-term Kashmir plan
could be put at risk.

257
00:16:22,458 --> 00:16:24,291
As for me, it's my job to warn you, sir.

258
00:16:24,375 --> 00:16:25,750
Yes, of course.

259
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:28,250
And my job is to tell the difference.

260
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:33,416
You focus on ISI operations,
not on General Musharraf.

261
00:16:36,166 --> 00:16:39,083
The new flight commander
isn't exactly giving off commander vibes.

262
00:16:39,791 --> 00:16:42,583
You never judge a jet's power
by the size of its body, Goofy.

263
00:16:43,333 --> 00:16:44,916
Getting a feeling from the mission?

264
00:16:47,333 --> 00:16:49,708
Bad weather above,
anti-aircraft guns below.

265
00:16:49,791 --> 00:16:50,875
There is danger everywhere.

266
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:52,708
Of course I'm feeling good about it

267
00:16:52,791 --> 00:16:54,000
Perfect.

268
00:16:54,083 --> 00:16:55,375
Happy landings, Goofy.

269
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:04,125
Trident taxy via link Alpha Runway
2-7-QNH-1-0-0-2.

270
00:17:04,208 --> 00:17:07,750
Link Alpha, Runway 2-7-1-0-0-2, copied.

271
00:17:07,833 --> 00:17:09,125
Trident in sequence.

272
00:17:11,541 --> 00:17:13,416
Trident sequence, monitored.

273
00:17:22,583 --> 00:17:23,500
Sir.

274
00:17:24,833 --> 00:17:28,000
Vanguard Control,
Trident Formation, ready to take off.

275
00:17:46,583 --> 00:17:48,208
These rolls were part of the briefing?

276
00:17:48,291 --> 00:17:50,291
Sir, that's Flying Officer Dhaliwal.

277
00:17:51,541 --> 00:17:52,541
Very talented.

278
00:17:53,708 --> 00:17:55,291
And a bit of a show-off too, sir.

279
00:18:09,750 --> 00:18:10,875
Can we go to the ops room?

280
00:18:12,375 --> 00:18:13,625
Sure, sir.

281
00:18:29,166 --> 00:18:31,458
Sir, would you be attending
the debrief today?

282
00:18:32,458 --> 00:18:33,500
On my first day?

283
00:18:34,750 --> 00:18:37,750
-I think today I'll just observe?
-Right, sir.

284
00:18:38,750 --> 00:18:40,250
Sir, message from Met Department.

285
00:18:40,333 --> 00:18:41,791
"Heavy cloud patch in Trident's route."

286
00:18:42,541 --> 00:18:44,250
-Sir?
-Safety first, always.

287
00:18:44,333 --> 00:18:46,333
Break RT silence. Alert them.

288
00:18:47,333 --> 00:18:48,958
Trident, Vanguard Control.

289
00:18:49,541 --> 00:18:51,916
Exercise caution
for large cloud build up.

290
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,833
There's heavy patch coming your way--

291
00:18:53,916 --> 00:18:55,333
RT silence, Khan.

292
00:18:55,416 --> 00:18:56,875
Whatever it is, I will handle it.

293
00:19:00,666 --> 00:19:02,250
Trident 2, Vanguard Control.

294
00:19:02,333 --> 00:19:04,500
Exercise caution
for large cloud buildup in sector.

295
00:19:04,583 --> 00:19:06,000
Zero-four-zero, 30 kilometers.

296
00:19:06,083 --> 00:19:07,291
Roger. Copy, Trident 2.

297
00:19:19,375 --> 00:19:21,583
RT silence, Goofy.
Do you want to gossip on channel 2?

298
00:19:21,666 --> 00:19:24,333
Dhali, what are you doing, man?
There's a cloud alert.

299
00:19:24,416 --> 00:19:26,041
Right now we're up in the air,
aren't we, Goofy?

300
00:19:26,125 --> 00:19:27,291
So just follow my lead.

301
00:19:27,375 --> 00:19:29,291
This is the semi-final mission.

302
00:19:29,375 --> 00:19:31,375
No matter what,
we will complete it on time.

303
00:19:37,291 --> 00:19:39,166
Vanguard Control, Trident 2,

304
00:19:39,250 --> 00:19:41,166
leader is not responding.
Going ahead as planned.

305
00:20:21,208 --> 00:20:22,750
Trident Formation,

306
00:20:22,833 --> 00:20:23,916
lost Joy on you.

307
00:20:34,916 --> 00:20:36,583
Trident Formation, confirm monitored.

308
00:21:08,625 --> 00:21:09,958
Shit!

309
00:21:12,541 --> 00:21:13,500
Dhali!

310
00:21:30,875 --> 00:21:32,708
Trident Formation, confirm ops normal.

311
00:21:32,791 --> 00:21:35,291
Trident Formation, confirm ops normal.

312
00:21:35,375 --> 00:21:37,041
Affirmative. Heading to the party.

313
00:21:38,916 --> 00:21:40,250
Close shave, boys.

314
00:21:40,333 --> 00:21:41,458
But the real mission starts now.

315
00:21:41,541 --> 00:21:43,375
And you have only 45 seconds.

316
00:21:43,958 --> 00:21:45,250
Go get those points.

317
00:22:21,750 --> 00:22:23,958
Trident Formation is approaching target.

318
00:22:29,125 --> 00:22:31,250
Mission completed.
Heading back to base.

319
00:22:32,083 --> 00:22:34,833
Sir, Trident Formation
is heading back to base.

320
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:38,875
I changed my mind, Chou.

321
00:22:38,958 --> 00:22:42,541
I… will attend the debriefing.

322
00:22:52,625 --> 00:22:55,041
-Sergeant, take the camera to the PIC.
-Sir.

323
00:22:58,958 --> 00:22:59,958
Are you okay?

324
00:23:03,625 --> 00:23:05,208
That was a bit much, don't you think?

325
00:23:06,958 --> 00:23:08,750
You felt good about it, didn't you?

326
00:23:18,583 --> 00:23:19,750
Goofy, why did you

327
00:23:20,791 --> 00:23:22,500
follow instead of aborting the mission?

328
00:23:22,583 --> 00:23:26,416
Sir, the leader asked me to follow,
so there was no option to abort.

329
00:23:27,125 --> 00:23:28,208
Textbook wingman call.

330
00:23:30,375 --> 00:23:31,208
Well done.

331
00:23:32,375 --> 00:23:34,541
And you? Ground orders were clear.

332
00:23:34,625 --> 00:23:36,375
So why did you

333
00:23:37,083 --> 00:23:38,666
take the risk of flying into the clouds?

334
00:23:39,500 --> 00:23:41,083
For 20 mission points, sir.

335
00:23:41,166 --> 00:23:45,125
The risk of collision for both pilots
was very high during cloud flying.

336
00:23:45,208 --> 00:23:46,166
Did you factor that in?

337
00:23:46,250 --> 00:23:47,750
Sir, we've flown together for a year.

338
00:23:47,833 --> 00:23:49,875
We completely trust each other, sir.

339
00:23:51,041 --> 00:23:52,250
And, suppose,

340
00:23:54,416 --> 00:23:56,041
while flying in the clouds,

341
00:23:56,541 --> 00:23:57,791
you became disoriented?

342
00:23:58,500 --> 00:24:00,166
We could've easily reoriented, sir.

343
00:24:01,083 --> 00:24:04,000
Only our squadron
has a global positioning system.

344
00:24:07,666 --> 00:24:08,500
Grounded.

345
00:24:10,875 --> 00:24:12,000
For one week.

346
00:24:12,875 --> 00:24:13,791
No sorties.

347
00:24:15,166 --> 00:24:16,083
Sorry, sir?

348
00:24:16,166 --> 00:24:18,500
For a week,
you will only perform ground duties.

349
00:24:19,083 --> 00:24:20,583
Bird clearance, paperwork…

350
00:24:20,666 --> 00:24:23,541
You'll interpret photos
from the other pilots' sorties.

351
00:24:23,625 --> 00:24:26,000
Pardon me, sir. But why?

352
00:24:26,083 --> 00:24:29,166
The mission needed to be completed,
and I only took a calculated risk.

353
00:24:29,250 --> 00:24:30,958
Sir, if we didn't do this,

354
00:24:31,541 --> 00:24:33,625
we would have lost, and the entire blame
would have fallen on Golden Arrows.

355
00:24:33,708 --> 00:24:35,500
It's as simple as that, sir.

356
00:24:35,583 --> 00:24:37,125
And, there was no other way, sir.

357
00:24:37,208 --> 00:24:38,666
Does everyone feel the same,

358
00:24:40,291 --> 00:24:41,291
that

359
00:24:42,291 --> 00:24:43,541
there was no other way?

360
00:24:43,625 --> 00:24:44,750
There was, sir.

361
00:24:45,375 --> 00:24:46,250
There was a way.

362
00:24:46,333 --> 00:24:47,708
Go on, Baldy. Explain.

363
00:24:48,291 --> 00:24:49,916
Sir, dogleg maneuver.

364
00:24:50,708 --> 00:24:52,250
You could have gone around the cloud.

365
00:24:55,583 --> 00:24:57,708
And the time
that would have gone into rerouting?

366
00:24:58,791 --> 00:24:59,875
Two minutes at the most.

367
00:24:59,958 --> 00:25:02,375
The length of the cloud
was ten kilometers.

368
00:25:02,458 --> 00:25:05,083
And a detour around the clouds…
that's 20 kilometers.

369
00:25:05,166 --> 00:25:08,250
What about the extra fuel
the detour would've cost?

370
00:25:10,125 --> 00:25:12,541
Sir, at a speed of 800 kmph,

371
00:25:12,625 --> 00:25:15,625
we probably used way more fuel
handling the cloud turbulence

372
00:25:16,416 --> 00:25:20,791
than the extra amount needed
to cover that ten-kilometer difference.

373
00:25:22,125 --> 00:25:25,416
I think dogleg was a safer
and more efficient option.

374
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:28,875
Clearly, what is safe for me

375
00:25:28,958 --> 00:25:30,666
is dangerous
for our "professor sahib" here.

376
00:25:30,750 --> 00:25:33,291
And it's fine. Every pilot
has their own risk-taking capability--

377
00:25:33,375 --> 00:25:34,666
So, you agree.

378
00:25:36,291 --> 00:25:37,583
That there was another way.

379
00:25:37,666 --> 00:25:40,083
Sir, in that moment,
it was just me up in the air.

380
00:25:40,166 --> 00:25:41,875
You weren't there and nor was he.

381
00:25:43,166 --> 00:25:45,708
And if it were wartime, sir,
would we still abort--

382
00:25:45,791 --> 00:25:47,833
Grounded for two weeks, Dhaliwal.

383
00:25:48,958 --> 00:25:51,375
Let's save the risk for a real war.

384
00:25:51,458 --> 00:25:53,666
There is no war going on right now.

385
00:26:29,916 --> 00:26:31,375
As-salamu alaykum, Chief.

386
00:26:31,458 --> 00:26:33,916
I have an urgent update to give.

387
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:35,333
Lieutenant General Aziz

388
00:26:35,416 --> 00:26:37,750
and Lieutenant General Mahmud
are both on the line.

389
00:26:38,500 --> 00:26:39,625
Tell me.

390
00:26:40,291 --> 00:26:41,750
Sir, as per the plan,

391
00:26:41,833 --> 00:26:46,875
soldiers from our 12NLI
have captured eight vacant Indian posts.

392
00:26:46,958 --> 00:26:48,333
But as they moved forward,

393
00:26:48,416 --> 00:26:52,541
they found many more hidden posts
we were not even aware of.

394
00:26:56,333 --> 00:26:59,333
It's clear that India
is guarding NH1 like a fortress.

395
00:26:59,416 --> 00:27:01,500
And now that
India is honoring the agreement

396
00:27:01,583 --> 00:27:03,416
and stepping down from all these posts,

397
00:27:03,500 --> 00:27:05,291
we should take full advantage
of this situation.

398
00:27:05,875 --> 00:27:07,500
I think we should take them all, sir.

399
00:27:07,583 --> 00:27:10,083
Hassan, to hold posts
across such a vast area,

400
00:27:10,166 --> 00:27:13,458
we will have to cancel the winter holidays
of 3,000 to 4,000 soldiers.

401
00:27:13,541 --> 00:27:16,166
We're already violating
the Simla Agreement

402
00:27:16,250 --> 00:27:17,458
by crossing the LoC in winter.

403
00:27:17,541 --> 00:27:21,500
Capturing 200 square kilometers of area
would be a major invasion.

404
00:27:21,583 --> 00:27:26,791
General Mahmud, do you set out
to capture Kashmir every day?

405
00:27:28,791 --> 00:27:29,791
No, sir.

406
00:27:31,500 --> 00:27:34,583
So, you'll never get
a better opportunity than this.

407
00:27:36,041 --> 00:27:37,875
-General Hassan.
-Yes, sir.

408
00:27:37,958 --> 00:27:40,750
Start preparing to capture
all those posts.

409
00:27:40,833 --> 00:27:43,083
Not even in their wildest dreams
would they imagine

410
00:27:43,166 --> 00:27:44,291
we could do something like this.

411
00:27:44,875 --> 00:27:47,958
In this operation, our audacity
will be our greatest strength.

412
00:27:48,541 --> 00:27:52,583
Start making a list of supplies.
I'm sending Tauqir Zia to you.

413
00:27:53,166 --> 00:27:56,708
-Long live Pakistan.
-Long live Pakistan, sir.

414
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:18,750
Dhali. I have some good news.

415
00:28:18,833 --> 00:28:22,208
The bombing squadron destroyed
Red Land's comms base.

416
00:28:22,291 --> 00:28:23,583
And we won the semi-finals.

417
00:28:24,416 --> 00:28:26,125
-I know.
-That's true.

418
00:28:27,208 --> 00:28:29,000
But I got my next posting.

419
00:28:30,041 --> 00:28:31,500
Mirage Squadron.

420
00:28:32,416 --> 00:28:33,458
Mir--

421
00:28:35,458 --> 00:28:38,375
Straight from Maruti to Ferrari.

422
00:28:42,208 --> 00:28:43,750
Congratulations, Sangy.

423
00:28:45,708 --> 00:28:50,791
Hopefully, there's no flight commander
there who punishes risk-taking.

424
00:28:51,625 --> 00:28:54,791
Let it go, Dhali.
You won us the semi-finals, man.

425
00:28:55,375 --> 00:28:57,083
Let's celebrate that today.

426
00:28:57,166 --> 00:28:59,000
Let's go. Drinks are on me tonight.

427
00:28:59,083 --> 00:29:00,875
No, man. Have fun.
I'm not in the mood. Thank you.

428
00:29:03,041 --> 00:29:04,125
It is unfair.

429
00:29:04,833 --> 00:29:07,750
Let's all talk to him together.
Let's see what Ahuja sir says.

430
00:29:07,833 --> 00:29:08,791
Yes, let's see.

431
00:29:09,416 --> 00:29:10,458
He's the Flight Commander.

432
00:29:10,541 --> 00:29:13,333
He'll do whatever he wants,
nobody can say a thing.

433
00:29:13,416 --> 00:29:16,166
So what if he's the flight commander?
We're bachelors too!

434
00:29:17,416 --> 00:29:18,666
Maybe we can't reason with him,

435
00:29:19,458 --> 00:29:20,708
but we can definitely mess with him.

436
00:29:28,041 --> 00:29:29,208
Let's go.

437
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:31,166
Where is Professor sahib?

438
00:29:31,750 --> 00:29:33,583
He'll be where he is every evening.

439
00:29:33,666 --> 00:29:34,541
Okay. Let's go then!

440
00:29:35,083 --> 00:29:36,666
Bala, do you love me or not?

441
00:29:38,083 --> 00:29:39,333
What kind of question is that?

442
00:29:39,416 --> 00:29:40,750
Of course I do.

443
00:29:40,833 --> 00:29:42,583
So, will you elope with me?

444
00:29:47,166 --> 00:29:49,916
Madhavi, I haven't even become
a flight lieutenant yet.

445
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:52,000
My training is still going on.

446
00:29:53,458 --> 00:29:55,166
Right now,
I don't think it's the right time.

447
00:29:55,250 --> 00:29:57,791
There's a lot of pressure at home.
Please try to understand.

448
00:30:02,541 --> 00:30:04,041
Bouncing?

449
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:05,875
You guys go.

450
00:30:05,958 --> 00:30:07,291
We are not asking.

451
00:30:11,500 --> 00:30:13,791
Madhavi, I will call you in an hour.

452
00:30:15,958 --> 00:30:16,916
Hello?

453
00:30:20,750 --> 00:30:22,291
It got cut.

454
00:30:49,541 --> 00:30:50,958
-Hello, ma'am.
-Hello, ma'am.

455
00:30:51,041 --> 00:30:52,750
Aren't you guys quite late?

456
00:30:53,500 --> 00:30:54,541
In the previous squadron,

457
00:30:54,625 --> 00:30:57,166
the bachelors had come to bounce
on the second day itself.

458
00:30:59,916 --> 00:31:01,166
Your team has arrived.

459
00:31:02,500 --> 00:31:03,666
Finally.

460
00:31:04,750 --> 00:31:05,708
Welcome home, boys.

461
00:31:06,375 --> 00:31:07,500
I don't drink.

462
00:31:08,250 --> 00:31:11,958
But I get others drunk.
This bar is all yours. Help yourself.

463
00:31:12,541 --> 00:31:13,625
You're in some form, huh, Dhali?

464
00:31:13,708 --> 00:31:16,458
-It's my second, man. It's his seventh.
-It's your seventh?

465
00:31:16,541 --> 00:31:18,875
It's all free while bouncing, no?
So he's drinking his heart's fill!

466
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:22,041
Doesn't want to pay for his drinks!

467
00:31:22,916 --> 00:31:23,958
Let's go.

468
00:31:25,250 --> 00:31:26,541
Start chopping.

469
00:31:30,791 --> 00:31:32,666
We will make my special dish.

470
00:31:34,708 --> 00:31:36,166
You want to eat, right?

471
00:31:37,083 --> 00:31:38,708
-Yes, ma'am.
-Then get started.

472
00:31:45,458 --> 00:31:48,041
What are you looking at?
This house belongs to Alka ma'am.

473
00:31:48,750 --> 00:31:50,083
I just live here.

474
00:31:51,250 --> 00:31:52,250
Come on.

475
00:31:56,708 --> 00:31:57,916
I'll chop the carrots.

476
00:31:58,625 --> 00:31:59,500
I'll chop the potatoes.

477
00:32:03,916 --> 00:32:06,041
Bro, it feels like
coming here to bounce has backfired.

478
00:32:07,750 --> 00:32:10,500
Honestly, these two seem
way more in sync than us.

479
00:32:11,041 --> 00:32:13,250
What's all this whispering?

480
00:32:14,125 --> 00:32:17,125
If you wanted to talk to each other,
why did you come here to bounce?

481
00:32:17,208 --> 00:32:18,333
Let's all hear it, come on.

482
00:32:19,083 --> 00:32:21,791
Sir, actually, Max was asking

483
00:32:21,875 --> 00:32:24,750
about the war game exercise finals--

484
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:28,083
Bouncing rule number one in this house,

485
00:32:29,083 --> 00:32:30,875
there will be no talk of flying.

486
00:32:32,166 --> 00:32:34,166
-No talk of flying, bro.
-There won't be.

487
00:32:34,250 --> 00:32:36,125
-Sir.
-Thank you, Sangy.

488
00:32:36,666 --> 00:32:38,083
But, ma'am, this is a very unfair rule.

489
00:32:38,166 --> 00:32:41,541
If this was a rule in my house,
I would never have become a fighter pilot.

490
00:32:42,333 --> 00:32:43,666
This conversation is allowed.

491
00:32:45,083 --> 00:32:47,541
Rajendra Dhaliwal, ma'am, my father…

492
00:32:48,166 --> 00:32:50,666
He was also in the Air Force.
Ground duty officer.

493
00:32:51,333 --> 00:32:53,416
And my mother was an amazing cook.

494
00:32:54,083 --> 00:32:56,791
So, all the fighter pilots used to come
to bounce at our house.

495
00:32:57,916 --> 00:33:00,333
Growing up listening
to all their flying stories,

496
00:33:00,416 --> 00:33:01,750
one day I got bitten by the bug.

497
00:33:01,833 --> 00:33:03,833
Where is Dad posted now?

498
00:33:03,916 --> 00:33:05,250
-He's retired.
-He's retired.

499
00:33:08,166 --> 00:33:09,916
Wing Commander Dhaliwal.

500
00:33:11,333 --> 00:33:12,458
'69 batch.

501
00:33:13,750 --> 00:33:15,250
Disciplined officer.

502
00:33:15,333 --> 00:33:18,000
-I'd met him briefly in Tezpur.
-Hey, one minute.

503
00:33:18,625 --> 00:33:22,958
Ahuja sir has a file on everyone.
But I don't know anything.

504
00:33:23,041 --> 00:33:26,541
So how did the rest of you catch this bug?

505
00:33:28,833 --> 00:33:29,916
-Yes?
-Sangy.

506
00:33:31,416 --> 00:33:35,333
Ma'am, where I come from, the only way
to get out of town is to join the army.

507
00:33:36,291 --> 00:33:39,333
My father, my grandfather,
both were in the army.

508
00:33:40,208 --> 00:33:42,708
But neither of them could fight in a war.

509
00:33:43,625 --> 00:33:47,208
So, I'm just trying to pay off that debt.

510
00:33:47,875 --> 00:33:52,083
Ma'am, he doesn't drink much, so he's
always caught between debt and duty.

511
00:34:09,666 --> 00:34:13,250
Ma'am, when you said "special,"
I had something else in mind.

512
00:34:13,333 --> 00:34:15,958
I never imagined pulao could be so good.

513
00:34:16,500 --> 00:34:17,541
What's in it?

514
00:34:18,416 --> 00:34:20,000
Thank you so much for the food, ma'am.

515
00:34:20,083 --> 00:34:23,791
But I have to leave now.
I have an urgent call to make.

516
00:34:23,875 --> 00:34:27,041
Well, who's going to wash the dishes?
Forgotten the tradition?

517
00:34:28,333 --> 00:34:31,208
By the way, Baldy,
you can call from here too.

518
00:34:31,291 --> 00:34:33,791
-We have an STD connection.
-Yes, do it.

519
00:34:34,666 --> 00:34:37,000
Sir, he wants to make
a private call from a public booth.

520
00:34:41,666 --> 00:34:42,875
You can go, Baldy.

521
00:34:43,791 --> 00:34:46,041
Dhali, you can do
Baldy's share of the dishes.

522
00:34:46,125 --> 00:34:47,208
Yes. Sure, ma'am.

523
00:34:47,916 --> 00:34:49,958
But who is she, Professor sahib?

524
00:34:50,750 --> 00:34:52,375
You're ditching
the entire squadron for her.

525
00:34:52,458 --> 00:34:55,208
No one, Dhali.
I have an urgent family call.

526
00:34:55,958 --> 00:34:58,458
See you tomorrow.
Thank you, sir. Thank you, ma'am.

527
00:34:58,541 --> 00:35:01,916
But what family emergency came up?

528
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:03,291
Dhali, wallet.

529
00:35:03,375 --> 00:35:04,916
I'm just taking out
her contact for everyone.

530
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:06,875
There must be
a photo of the person in here.

531
00:35:06,958 --> 00:35:09,000
-I'm just checking, man.
-Don't do it.

532
00:35:09,083 --> 00:35:11,750
-Hey, wait a minute. Here it is. I see it.
-Dhali!

533
00:35:24,583 --> 00:35:25,666
I'll get the first aid kit.

534
00:35:25,750 --> 00:35:26,625
Oh, no, ma'am.

535
00:35:26,708 --> 00:35:28,208
-I'm completely fine. I'm absolutely okay.
-No, you're not.

536
00:35:28,291 --> 00:35:29,916
I am absolutely fine, ma'am.

537
00:35:39,875 --> 00:35:40,958
Sir.

538
00:36:05,708 --> 00:36:10,666
Mian sahib, I can say with certainty
that this fellow is up to no good.

539
00:36:11,416 --> 00:36:13,875
You should not trust him too much.

540
00:36:18,833 --> 00:36:19,833
General.

541
00:36:21,750 --> 00:36:23,958
We were just about to start. Come.

542
00:36:29,208 --> 00:36:31,875
Sir, you called me so urgently.
Is everything all right?

543
00:36:33,583 --> 00:36:35,291
Butt sahib has some concerns.

544
00:36:37,166 --> 00:36:39,458
I thought I'd take this opportunity
to also have breakfast with you.

545
00:36:40,708 --> 00:36:44,583
I've already had breakfast, Mian sahib.
But I'll have some fruit.

546
00:36:45,583 --> 00:36:49,375
Tell me, Butt sahib.
What are the ISI's concerns?

547
00:36:50,375 --> 00:36:51,958
The concern is

548
00:36:52,041 --> 00:36:55,916
why are we cancelling the winter holidays
of thousands of soldiers of the X Corps

549
00:36:56,583 --> 00:36:58,166
and sending them to Skardu?

550
00:36:58,750 --> 00:37:02,916
Such heavy troop movement
along the LoC during peace talks?

551
00:37:03,625 --> 00:37:04,833
It's a bit alarming.

552
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:21,916
Sir, we have intel that some Mujahideen
are planning to infiltrate the valley

553
00:37:22,750 --> 00:37:25,333
in order to derail the peace talks.

554
00:37:27,041 --> 00:37:30,750
As ISI Chief, perhaps you didn't get
this piece of intel.

555
00:37:32,541 --> 00:37:36,416
Sir, to maintain peace at the border,
many leaves have been canceled.

556
00:37:36,500 --> 00:37:39,875
Many have been deployed along the border.

557
00:37:40,833 --> 00:37:42,666
So this means you are

558
00:37:43,916 --> 00:37:45,791
doing this to protect
the security of the peace talks?

559
00:37:47,375 --> 00:37:48,833
Yes, sir. Of course.

560
00:37:53,791 --> 00:37:55,000
Very thoughtful.

561
00:37:55,083 --> 00:37:59,666
Sir, the army and the government have been
locked in a tug-of-war for a long time.

562
00:38:00,750 --> 00:38:02,166
I want to put an end to this.

563
00:38:03,166 --> 00:38:06,875
I want to show the public
that Rawalpindi and Islamabad

564
00:38:07,458 --> 00:38:08,916
can play on the same pitch, sir.

565
00:38:10,041 --> 00:38:11,458
We can work together.

566
00:38:16,541 --> 00:38:18,666
See, Butt sahib. I told you, didn't I?

567
00:38:20,166 --> 00:38:22,000
There's no need to worry
about General Musharraf.

568
00:38:23,375 --> 00:38:24,583
He is playing on our team.

569
00:38:43,541 --> 00:38:45,958
I am sorry, ma'am. I've double-checked.

570
00:38:46,041 --> 00:38:48,083
Your name is not
on the approved visitor list.

571
00:38:48,166 --> 00:38:51,125
Sir, please just connect me to Bala once…

572
00:38:51,208 --> 00:38:52,875
I mean, put me through
to Flying Officer Bal Reddy.

573
00:38:52,958 --> 00:38:54,166
He'll explain everything to you.

574
00:38:54,250 --> 00:38:56,833
Sorry, madam. An exercise is going on.
Nothing can be done right now.

575
00:38:57,958 --> 00:39:01,000
Then let me talk to the CO.
Tony sir, right?

576
00:39:26,333 --> 00:39:27,458
Sorry, sir.

577
00:39:28,333 --> 00:39:30,333
I had no idea

578
00:39:31,416 --> 00:39:32,875
Madhavi was coming here.

579
00:39:37,083 --> 00:39:38,458
-Chou.
-Sir?

580
00:39:39,250 --> 00:39:42,000
Can she be accommodated
in the VIP guesthouse?

581
00:39:42,791 --> 00:39:43,791
Fully occupied, sir.

582
00:39:49,083 --> 00:39:49,916
Sir…

583
00:39:51,958 --> 00:39:53,625
she can stay with us.

584
00:39:56,458 --> 00:39:58,416
Alka and I will be happy to host Madhavi.

585
00:40:01,041 --> 00:40:04,666
Okay then.
Baldy, you can get back to work.

586
00:40:05,791 --> 00:40:07,041
Yes, sir.

587
00:40:19,250 --> 00:40:22,416
The siren for the war game finals
can go off anytime. We need to be ready.

588
00:40:22,500 --> 00:40:24,833
Our target will be
Red Land's key airbase.

589
00:40:25,625 --> 00:40:29,583
But this time we'll take photos
after the bombing, not before,

590
00:40:30,250 --> 00:40:34,041
to find out
if the bombs hit their target or not.

591
00:40:34,125 --> 00:40:38,833
Battle damage assessment is far more
dangerous than photo recon flying.

592
00:40:39,458 --> 00:40:42,000
Because we won't have
the element of surprise.

593
00:40:42,625 --> 00:40:44,833
Their radars will be waiting for us.

594
00:40:44,916 --> 00:40:46,625
And they'll certainly have
surface-to-air missiles.

595
00:40:50,666 --> 00:40:54,833
So this time, we will try a new strategy.

596
00:40:54,916 --> 00:40:59,416
This strategy will serve us
not only in a war game, but also in war.

597
00:41:09,416 --> 00:41:11,541
If this is the enemy's radar screen…

598
00:41:13,916 --> 00:41:15,750
how many dots will be visible on it?

599
00:41:16,916 --> 00:41:18,916
Sir, six.

600
00:41:24,666 --> 00:41:26,291
Exactly.

601
00:41:26,875 --> 00:41:29,000
Six jets in close formation.

602
00:41:29,083 --> 00:41:33,500
So close that it should appear as
one big dot on the enemy's radar screen.

603
00:41:34,041 --> 00:41:38,041
And the enemy should think
it's a large transport aircraft.

604
00:41:38,125 --> 00:41:40,500
We will fly in close formation
up to the target.

605
00:41:41,083 --> 00:41:44,458
And at the last minute,
we'll break formation and click photos.

606
00:41:44,541 --> 00:41:48,375
And after clicking photos,
before their interceptors arrive,

607
00:41:48,458 --> 00:41:50,375
we will have crossed the mock LoC.

608
00:41:51,208 --> 00:41:53,833
Into friendly skies. Clear?

609
00:41:57,750 --> 00:41:59,958
What's wrong, boys? Too risky?

610
00:42:02,000 --> 00:42:04,916
Dhali, I was going to reinstate you.

611
00:42:07,875 --> 00:42:10,875
-But okay. If you can't, then--
-No. We can, sir.

612
00:42:11,500 --> 00:42:12,375
We will do it.

613
00:42:13,333 --> 00:42:15,875
-Come again?
-We'll do it, sir!

614
00:42:17,375 --> 00:42:18,333
Good.

615
00:42:20,375 --> 00:42:22,708
And, Dhali, this time
you won't be flying with Goofy.

616
00:42:25,166 --> 00:42:28,750
I've shuffled everyone's wingmen.
Check the flying program board.

617
00:42:52,500 --> 00:42:55,583
Baldy, call in position.
I'm at 700, match my speed.

618
00:43:00,833 --> 00:43:03,875
-In position.
-Now maintain position, Baldy.

619
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:17,208
Sangy joining up. Goofy call in position.

620
00:43:18,166 --> 00:43:19,583
Goofy joining up.

621
00:43:21,666 --> 00:43:23,625
-Teekay joining up.
-Max joining up.

622
00:43:24,375 --> 00:43:26,916
Tridents, Diamond formation is complete.

623
00:43:27,416 --> 00:43:30,250
Let's maintain speed.
Let's not mess it up, guys.

624
00:43:34,083 --> 00:43:36,500
Baldy, too close.
You're falling behind, man.

625
00:43:36,583 --> 00:43:38,208
Sorry, Sangy. Maintaining.

626
00:43:38,291 --> 00:43:40,500
Baldy, it's not a school bus.
Maintain 700.

627
00:43:40,583 --> 00:43:42,833
-Dhali, slow down and match Baldy's speed?
-Negative.

628
00:43:42,916 --> 00:43:45,166
The mission also has to be carried out
at this speed, right?

629
00:43:45,250 --> 00:43:47,666
-Baldy, increase your speed.
-Roger.

630
00:43:47,750 --> 00:43:48,916
Increasing.

631
00:43:56,333 --> 00:43:57,708
Formation stable at 700.

632
00:43:58,791 --> 00:43:59,791
Ready to turn left.

633
00:44:00,750 --> 00:44:01,958
Baldy, be on guard.

634
00:44:03,541 --> 00:44:05,708
Tridents, pan left 0-5-3.

635
00:44:11,041 --> 00:44:15,458
Formation stable at turn.
Accelerate to 750 now!

636
00:44:16,041 --> 00:44:18,000
Baldy, what are you doing?
You're falling behind again.

637
00:44:19,000 --> 00:44:22,208
Baldy, we're not even close to Mach 1!
Maintain 750.

638
00:44:23,083 --> 00:44:24,291
I'm trying.

639
00:44:24,375 --> 00:44:25,500
Dhali, why aren't you listening?

640
00:44:25,583 --> 00:44:29,083
-Let's maintain speed with Baldy.
-Negative. Let's stick to 750.

641
00:44:29,166 --> 00:44:31,083
Everyone, 750 now!

642
00:44:31,791 --> 00:44:35,291
Baldy, what are you doing, man?
We'll collide. Teekay, peel off, now!

643
00:44:35,375 --> 00:44:37,291
-Teekay peeling off!
-Arrows, peel off!

644
00:44:37,375 --> 00:44:39,208
Abort! Abort! Abort!

645
00:44:45,916 --> 00:44:47,375
Come on, guys!

646
00:45:06,333 --> 00:45:07,750
Sit, sit, sit, Please.

647
00:45:09,583 --> 00:45:11,833
What happened?
Why is everyone in such a bad mood?

648
00:45:13,708 --> 00:45:17,375
It was a practice sortie,
not a war exercise mission.

649
00:45:18,208 --> 00:45:19,958
Another round for everyone, please.

650
00:45:21,291 --> 00:45:22,375
Sangy?

651
00:45:23,500 --> 00:45:26,250
We celebrate life
after close calls, don't we?

652
00:45:26,333 --> 00:45:30,000
We do celebrate, sir.
But this call was way too close.

653
00:45:31,458 --> 00:45:33,125
We almost collided.

654
00:45:35,666 --> 00:45:38,791
It was probably the first time
we were flying in a formation of six.

655
00:45:38,875 --> 00:45:42,833
And so, it became a little difficult
to stay in sync with each other.

656
00:45:42,916 --> 00:45:44,875
No, sir. I am to blame for this.

657
00:45:46,875 --> 00:45:48,125
Sir, it was my fault.

658
00:45:48,708 --> 00:45:49,791
I…

659
00:45:51,125 --> 00:45:54,708
I was having trouble
matching Dhali's speed.

660
00:45:56,875 --> 00:45:59,875
Sir, the problem…
was the choice of exercise.

661
00:46:01,125 --> 00:46:02,333
Okay.

662
00:46:03,875 --> 00:46:06,625
Sir, Ahuja sir makes us do
an extremely risky exercise.

663
00:46:07,333 --> 00:46:09,291
Which is fine with me. I'm up for it.

664
00:46:10,125 --> 00:46:13,583
But then,
to suddenly shuffle our wingmen, sir.

665
00:46:15,000 --> 00:46:16,750
How will perfection be achieved, sir?

666
00:46:20,250 --> 00:46:21,416
Suddenly?

667
00:46:26,625 --> 00:46:30,166
When you encounter a technical glitch
in the air, it happens suddenly.

668
00:46:31,208 --> 00:46:34,000
When the decision to eject has to be made,

669
00:46:34,083 --> 00:46:37,250
no one leaves home thinking that
they will have to eject today.

670
00:46:39,041 --> 00:46:40,375
It happens suddenly.

671
00:46:41,250 --> 00:46:45,375
I haven't called Ahuja here
for your routine exercises.

672
00:46:47,000 --> 00:46:50,583
I've called him
so he can prepare you for war.

673
00:46:52,625 --> 00:46:54,333
Because when war breaks out,

674
00:46:56,250 --> 00:46:57,958
even that happens suddenly.

675
00:46:59,250 --> 00:47:01,875
If you guys think of yourselves
as fighter pilots,

676
00:47:04,500 --> 00:47:07,333
then have the courage
to accept a challenge,

677
00:47:08,083 --> 00:47:09,583
and not just complain about it.

678
00:47:11,333 --> 00:47:13,708
We're meant to be razor blades. Right?

679
00:47:13,791 --> 00:47:15,000
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

680
00:47:16,958 --> 00:47:19,083
Then bloody behave like one.

681
00:48:06,291 --> 00:48:08,791
-Long live Pakistan.
-Long live Pakistan.

682
00:48:08,875 --> 00:48:10,291
Welcome to Skardu, sir.

683
00:48:11,750 --> 00:48:12,708
Hassan,

684
00:48:13,833 --> 00:48:17,375
what are Mujahideen doing
at this army base?

685
00:48:18,916 --> 00:48:20,166
Come, sir.

686
00:48:21,291 --> 00:48:23,208
I'll explain it to you.

687
00:48:40,291 --> 00:48:44,833
So the Pakistan Army
will now work with Mujahideen?

688
00:48:46,916 --> 00:48:48,416
Do they seem like Mujahideen to you?

689
00:48:51,875 --> 00:48:53,375
Then that's how they'll seem
to the Indians too.

690
00:48:54,583 --> 00:48:58,708
Then, it will also seem to them that
the Pakistan Army has no role in this.

691
00:48:59,750 --> 00:49:03,000
Because we will
only speak to them in Pashto.

692
00:49:03,083 --> 00:49:06,208
But the truth is,
these are not Mujahideen.

693
00:49:06,750 --> 00:49:09,500
They are 2,000 soldiers of our 12 NLI.

694
00:49:09,583 --> 00:49:11,875
-Naara-e-Takbeer!
-Allah-hu-Akbar!

695
00:49:11,958 --> 00:49:13,791
-Naara-e-Takbeer!
-Allah-hu-Akbar!

696
00:49:13,875 --> 00:49:16,083
-Naara-e-Takbeer!
-Allah-hu-Akbar!

697
00:49:16,166 --> 00:49:18,833
-Naara-e-Takbeer!
-Allah-hu-Akbar!

698
00:49:18,916 --> 00:49:21,166
-Naara-e-Takbeer!
-Allah-hu-Akbar!

699
00:49:26,916 --> 00:49:28,000
Sir.

700
00:49:29,083 --> 00:49:31,583
You briefed me on eight posts
and 100 soldiers.

701
00:49:31,666 --> 00:49:35,875
The preparations underway in Skardu…
it's no less than a war, sir.

702
00:49:38,750 --> 00:49:40,583
General Zia, you look quite refreshed.

703
00:49:40,666 --> 00:49:43,333
Looks like fresh mountain air
suits you rather well.

704
00:49:51,041 --> 00:49:55,125
General Zia, the more posts we capture,

705
00:49:55,208 --> 00:49:57,500
the more pressure we can put on India.

706
00:49:57,583 --> 00:50:01,208
Undoubtedly, the height advantage
will allow us to take on the Indian Army.

707
00:50:01,291 --> 00:50:04,500
But what if they involve their air force?

708
00:50:08,958 --> 00:50:13,125
We have double-checked
with the German and Russian Air Forces.

709
00:50:13,208 --> 00:50:18,000
In that terrain, at those heights,
no Air Force in the world can operate!

710
00:50:18,750 --> 00:50:20,083
And this is a proven fact.

711
00:50:20,166 --> 00:50:21,750
Sir, still I feel

712
00:50:21,833 --> 00:50:25,875
our soldiers on the peaks
should be armed with Stinger missiles.

713
00:50:26,791 --> 00:50:27,916
"Mujahideen."

714
00:50:28,875 --> 00:50:32,166
Not our soldiers, Mujahideen, General Zia.

715
00:50:34,750 --> 00:50:37,750
Aren't you the DGMO?
Give them the Stingers.

716
00:50:38,750 --> 00:50:39,708
What's the big deal?

717
00:50:40,416 --> 00:50:42,750
Sir, Stinger missiles
are not regular weapons.

718
00:50:42,833 --> 00:50:46,291
For large-scale mobilization,
we will need the PM's approval.

719
00:51:01,500 --> 00:51:03,583
You worry too much, Tauqir.

720
00:51:06,583 --> 00:51:09,875
If we are to snatch Kashmir from India,

721
00:51:11,416 --> 00:51:14,333
we'll have to put in
a little bit of effort, won't we?

722
00:51:15,666 --> 00:51:21,041
When the time comes, I'll get Mian sahib
to sign off on everything.

723
00:51:25,000 --> 00:51:26,833
We have to seize Kashmir.

724
00:56:15,916 --> 00:56:20,916
Subtitle translation by: Ajay Singh

